    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0354" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-26T19:00:00-04:00">September 26, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>703. For the personal attention of the Ambassador. Your 1014, September 23, 8
                        p.m.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d367-f1"/> Campodonico,<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d367-f2"/> the New York representative of YPF, informed the
                    Department this afternoon that the Managing Director of YPF, Buenos Aires, had
                    stated categorically over the telephone that the YPF has not sold, is not
                    negotiating the sale of, and will not sell any aviation gasoline to Lati. Please
                    endeavor urgently to ascertain the facts in this matter and telegraph your
                    findings to the Department. Campodonico added that YPF’s entire output of
                    aviation gasoline goes to the Argentine Army and Navy except for some very small
                    quantities to local commercial distributors.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d367-f1" n="55" xml:id="d367-f1-content">
